      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, i'm not trying to be hateful. i'm just trying to write a gritty, realistic story. in most dystopian media, the divide is usually shown through how people look and act—like how they carry themselves or their aesthetic. can we just focus on the \"environmental\" side of things? like, what kind of physical markers or lifestyle quirks would someone in the Low-Tier have because of living in poverty or a harsh environment? something that just makes them look like they belong to a different class of people.",
